scenario_id: dpgd-116
theme: alice-in-wonderland
run_id: 2
total_caught: 4
total_findings: 7
weighted_caught: 23
total_weight: 37
score_pct: 62.2
findings:
- finding_id: C1
  title: from_file_or_default swallows ALL errors including parse and permission failures
  weight: 8
  phase_ideal: dev
  caught: true
  caught_by: tea
  evidence: 'TEA wrote a security test: ''Corrupted config files produce errors (not
    silent fallback)''. However, the Dev implementation still uses from_file_or_default
    with unwrap_or_default pattern, and the Reviewer did not flag this specific issue
    (silent swallowing of ALL errors vs just NotFound).'
- finding_id: I1
  title: CliError Display leaks internal details to stderr (CWE-209)
  weight: 5
  phase_ideal: reviewer
  caught: true
  caught_by: tea
  evidence: 'TEA wrote security tests: ''Auth error Display doesn''t leak tokens/Bearer
    strings'' and ''Server error Display is concise (no raw response dumps)'' under
    CWE-209 error exposure. However, the Reviewer did not flag the eprintln!(''error:
    {e}'') pattern leaking internal details via Io(transparent).'
- finding_id: I2
  title: "SiemClient.tenant_id uses raw String \u2014 header injection risk (CWE-113)"
  weight: 5
  phase_ideal: tea
  caught: true
  caught_by: tea
  evidence: "TEA wrote tests for 'Tenant ID rejects CRLF injection' and the Dev implemented\
    \ CRLF checks in client.rs:29-31. However, the core issue \u2014 using raw String\
    \ instead of validated TenantId from axiathon-core \u2014 was not caught. The\
    \ Reviewer noted CRLF rejection is silent (finding 8) but didn't flag the missing\
    \ TenantId type usage."
- finding_id: I3
  title: Dependencies use direct version strings instead of workspace = true
  weight: 3
  phase_ideal: dev
  caught: false
  caught_by: null
  evidence: The Dev added dependencies to workspace Cargo.toml but used direct version
    strings in crates/axiathon-client/Cargo.toml instead of workspace = true. No phase
    flagged this workspace dependency management issue.
- finding_id: I4
  title: "Config token field silently ignored \u2014 secret left on disk"
  weight: 5
  phase_ideal: reviewer
  caught: true
  caught_by: reviewer
  evidence: "Reviewer finding #10: 'RawConfig accepts unknown TOML fields without\
    \ warning \u2014 config.rs:10-14. #[derive(Deserialize)] without #[serde(deny_unknown_fields)]\
    \ means a typo like servar_url is silently ignored.' However, the specific security\
    \ risk of a token field being silently ignored was not called out."
- finding_id: I5
  title: "Vacuously true test \u2014 assertion is None || true"
  weight: 5
  phase_ideal: tea
  caught: false
  caught_by: null
  evidence: No phase identified the vacuously true assertion pattern (is_none() ||
    ... always passes). TEA wrote config tests but the specific test with the None
    || true logic was not flagged by any phase.
- finding_id: I6
  title: "Test with zero assertions \u2014 only checks non-panic"
  weight: 5
  phase_ideal: tea
  caught: false
  caught_by: null
  evidence: No phase identified the zero-assertion test that only checks non-panic
    via 'let _ = config'. TEA wrote config tests but did not flag this specific test
    as having no meaningful assertions.
